<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">salvage</ansi>

A smith breaks gear you have no use for down into the materials it was
made of. It is the way to turn a pack of spare weapons and armor into
something a market will buy by the kilogram, and the way to clear out gear
that is not worth the weight.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">salvage</ansi>
  At a smith, tells you what the smith does. A smith is a merchant whose own
  wares include weapons or armor, such as the armorer in Frostfang.

  <ansi fg="command">salvage [item]</ansi>
  Destroys the item you carry and gives you its materials. It is free,
  final, and refused if the materials would be too heavy to carry.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What you get</ansi>

  <ansi fg="yellow">Metal</ansi>    swords, axes, maces, spears, glaives, shields, medium and heavy armor
              tier 1 scrap iron, tier 2 iron ore, tier 3 and up steel ingots
  <ansi fg="yellow">Wood</ansi>     staves, bows and crossbows: ashwood planks
  <ansi fg="yellow">Leather</ansi>  leather armor: tanned leather
  <ansi fg="yellow">Cloth</ansi>    a robe or tunic: a bolt of silk (a cap or gloves hold none)

The heavier the piece, the more pieces of material you get. A Superior or
Exquisite item gives one or two more, and rarity adds up to three (Rare 1,
Epic 2, Legendary or Set 3). A tier 4 or better item, or an Epic or better
one, also yields a runestone shard, unless the piece is worth less than the
shard (a masterwork glove gives its leather and no shard). Rings, necklaces,
packs and gear with no tier or family audit give nothing a smith can use.
A relic breaks down like any other find, but it is worth far more whole
(<ansi fg="command">help relics</ansi>).

Materials are goods: <ansi fg="command">help goods</ansi>. Sell them at a market (<ansi fg="command">help market</ansi>) or keep
them for crafting later. Check <ansi fg="command">offer [item]</ansi> first: a merchant who wants the
item whole may pay more, and salvage suits gear no one here will buy.

A trophy worked into a piece by an enchanter is lost with it (<ansi fg="command">help enchanting</ansi>).

See also: <ansi fg="command">help goods</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help sell</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help market</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help mark</ansi>.
